{"type":"standard","title":"Oi language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Oi language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q13018626","titles":{"canonical":"Oi_language","normalized":"Oi language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Oi language</span></span>"},"pageid":19188625,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Oi_language.jpg/330px-Oi_language.jpg","width":330,"height":543},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5a/Oi_language.jpg","width":1138,"height":1873},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1330658631","tid":"a88ca073-e746-11f0-b6c1-b0cfe8f470b1","timestamp":"2026-01-01T19:18:31Z","description":"Austroasiatic language spoken in Laos","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oi_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oi_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oi_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Oi_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oi_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Oi_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oi_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Oi_language"}},"extract":"Oi is an Austroasiatic dialect cluster of Attapeu Province, southern Laos. The dominant variety is Oy proper, with 11,000 speakers who are 80% monolinguals. The Jeng (Cheng) speak the same language but are ethnically distinct. Speakers follow traditional religions.","extract_html":"<p><b>Oi</b> is an Austroasiatic dialect cluster of Attapeu Province, southern Laos. The dominant variety is Oy proper, with 11,000 speakers who are 80% monolinguals. The Jeng (Cheng) speak the same language but are ethnically distinct. Speakers follow traditional religions.</p>"}